  "review": {
    "audio": "The condition-variable worker holds the state mutex during synthesis, clears processing before notifying, and releases the lock atomically on the next wait. Its phase sequence preserves the tested exact long-run 32000-Hz schedule. Shutdown still joins before freeing worker resources.",
    "residency": "The ownership pass completes before invalidation/unload. Metadata aliases are visited before cache deletion. Static patch resources retain their own shared_ptr; player/keep directories, registry-backed raw skeletons and the official Kafei raw backup remain protected.",
    "heap_and_messages": "The native heap helper publishes pointers only after both allocations succeed; tests inject either allocation failure. Message allocation checks multiplication/addition extents and zeros the extra sentinel storage.",
    "fatal_shutdown": "Native fatal archive, message and heap failures now call the dedicated BlinkyAbortProcess bridge after displaying the existing error. This delegates process termination to native_runtime's Fatal/svcExitProcess path without freeing libctru heaps underneath the live GSP thread. Desktop exits and the nonfatal Messagebox_ShowErrorBox are preserved. Host failure-injection tests require all four message/heap failure paths to invoke the bridge.",
    "originality": "Only replaced native implementations are new contributions; the direct API edits are categorized D, exact upstream restoration C, and every containing MM file retains its official upstream base attribution. No exclusive-originality or clean-room certification is claimed."
  }
